-# USR-09: how the pages look, before the account button. A popover, as the
  account menu is: it opens and closes without a script. Each choice is a
  form of its own, sent with a full load of the page, so that the menu is
  closed and the map drawn anew; the button's name holds the present choice.
%button.header-button.theme-button{ type: "button", popovertarget: "theme-menu" }
  = render "theme_icon", name: user.theme, size: 20
  %span.visually-hidden= t(".button", theme: enum_name(User, :theme, user.theme))
.theme-menu#theme-menu{ popover: "auto", role: "group", aria: { label: t(".label") } }
  - User.themes.each_key do |name|
    = button_to theme_path, method: :patch, params: { theme: name },
      aria: { current: ("true" if user.theme == name) }, form: { data: { turbo: false } } do
      = render "theme_icon", name: name, size: 18
      = enum_name(User, :theme, name)
